# ───────────────────────────── Epic RPF — .gitignore ─────────────────────────────
# Goal: a fresh `git clone` contains EXACTLY what's needed to compile the program
# (and to build the installer) and nothing else — no build output, no backups, no
# multi-gigabyte scratch. After cloning you can build it just like we do:
#
#   dotnet build EpicRpf.slnx -c Debug                                   # the app
#   CodeWalker\_build.bat                                                # the bundled CodeWalker editor
#   powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File tools\build-installer.ps1   # the installer
#
# What IS committed on purpose (do NOT add these): src\ (all source + wwwroot, incl. the
# Monaco/three libs), libs\ (the prebuilt CodeWalker.Core.dll + strings.txt +
# ShadersGen9Conversion.xml that src\Directory.Build.props references — the app will NOT
# compile without it), CodeWalker\ source, skel\ runtime data, tools\, and
# installer\EpicRpf.iss (so the installer can be rebuilt too).
#
# EXCEPTION: the archive-lock engine (see below) is deliberately excluded from src\, so a
# fresh clone of THIS repo will NOT compile as-is — Bridge.cs, GameFs.cs, ArchiveFixer.cs and
# rpfcli's Program.cs all reference RpfLock/AppSecret/AdminKey. That's intentional: the lock
# feature isn't open-sourced. Building a full app requires those 3 files from a private copy.

# ── .NET build output (regenerated by `dotnet build` / publish) ───────────────────
bin/
obj/
*.user
*.suo
.vs/

# ── Distributables (regenerated by tools\build-installer.ps1) ─────────────────────
#    The self-contained publish AND every EpicRpf-Setup-<ver>.exe installer.
/dist/

# ── WebView2 Evergreen bootstrapper (auto-downloaded by build-installer.ps1) ──────
/installer/redist/

# ── Backups & scratch — not part of the program ───────────────────────────────────
/backups/
/_modwork/
*.bak
*.orig
*.old

# ── Lock system secrets / artefacts (NEVER commit) ────────────────────────────────
#    The admin private key opens any locked file without a password; lock sidecars are
#    per-archive metadata that live next to the user's .rpf files, not in the repo.
*.epickey
*.epclk

# ── Archive-lock ENGINE source (NEVER commit — not open-sourced) ──────────────────
#    The lock/unlock crypto itself (RpfLock), the baked app secret + admin public key
#    (AppSecret), and the admin RSA keypair helper (AdminKey). Keeping these out of git
#    means the algorithm and the baked secret material never end up in the repo/history —
#    only a private local copy of these 3 files can build the lock feature. See the note
#    at the top of this file.
src/App.Core/RpfLock.cs
src/App.Core/AppSecret.cs
src/App.Core/AdminKeys.cs

# ── Decompiled CodeWalker.Core reference (read-only; not built, not shipped) ───────
#    The app compiles against the prebuilt libs\CodeWalker.Core.dll, NOT this folder.
/_ref/

# ── IDE / OS junk ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.idea/
*.DotSettings.user
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
